        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0397" n="327" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg327"/>

                <head>No. 171.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr.
                    Sargent.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-01-12"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 12,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 74.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging the receipt of your very
                    interesting and instructive dispatch No. 87, of the 18th ultimo, in which you
                    give an account of the method in which it is proposed to accomplish the
                    exclusion of American pork from Germany, I have to request you to lose no
                    occasion to compass the abandonment of the restrictive and unjust measures now
                    proposed.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
